{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when","id":933145,"title":"What happens when....?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-17T16:42:59-07:00","id":933145,"title":"What happens when....?","content":"A human attempts to completely drain a vampire?\u200b<br /> <br /> i currently play 1e so i know a vampire can gain blood potency by drinking everything from another vampire with higher blood potency than their own but what if a human tries to do it? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T17:57:39-07:00","id":933170,"title":"","content":"A couple things. Giving your thread a title which links to the question will usually get you more views. <br /> <br /> To answer your question. I do believe it's not possible. Vampires don't bleed vitae. The vitae doesn't leave their body unless a vampire takes it, or they will it to flow. Otherwise it hides within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T17:58:52-07:00","id":933172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when#post933145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A human attempts to completely drain a vampire?\u200b<br /> i currently play 1e so i know a vampire can gain blood potency by drinking everything from another vampire with higher blood potency than their own but what if a human tries to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans aren't equipped to do it. Vitae doesn't permeates the vampiric body like blood does the human one, it resides around the heart, the older the vampire, the more concentrated it is. Vitae moves at the whim of the vampire, even with the Blush of life active, the warmth is but a pale imitation of the actual bodily fluid. Even Ghouldom is granted at the behest of a vampire, not merely at the act of drinking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T18:18:21-07:00","id":933179,"title":"","content":"Assuming the vampire allows itself to be drained (as previously mentioned) you'd have a vitae addicted human who is currently a thrall bound in one or more stages of a vinculum to the vampire whose vitae they drank. Meanwhile, you have an exsanguinated vampire likely to succumb to a starvation induced frenzy at any moment. Fun fun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T19:01:01-07:00","id":933196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933179#post933179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the vampire allows itself to be drained (as previously mentioned) you'd have a vitae addicted human who is currently a thrall bound in one or more stages of a vinculum to the vampire whose vitae they drank. Meanwhile, you have an exsanguinated vampire likely to succumb to a starvation induced frenzy at any moment. Fun fun...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat if the vampire was trapped being impaled to the floor by a spiked ceiling, would the newly thralled human feel compelled to release the vampire or simply keep drinking or would he be able to decide to finish off the vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T19:32:44-07:00","id":933207,"title":"","content":"If the vampire was impaled, he wouldn't be conscious to will his vitae to flow, so the human gets nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T23:46:18-07:00","id":933285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933196#post933196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhat if the vampire was trapped being impaled to the floor by a spiked ceiling, would the newly thralled human feel compelled to release the vampire or simply keep drinking or would he be able to decide to finish off the vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the vinculum requires that the blood bound roll for a breaking point when they act against the interests of whoever has bound them. So the human could do it, but it would require a very lucky dice roll or a very solid sense of self (high as hell integrity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T04:56:52-07:00","id":933365,"title":"","content":"Vampires can forceablly drain another Kindred's Vitae, so I don't think the, it doesn't leave the vampires body unless they want it to is a valid argument.<br /> <br /> Note, its not enough to drain a vampires Vitae to commit diablerie. You need to continue to drink, draining a vampires health levels. Mortals can't dialberize a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T05:49:30-07:00","id":933380,"title":"","content":"Actually, a human forcefully draining a vampire is one of the legendary origins of VII. At least, its one of the three in the VII covenant book. I think there's a total of five origin stories for VII now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T06:35:04-07:00","id":933393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933380#post933380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, a human forcefully draining a vampire is one of the legendary origins of VII. At least, its one of the three in the VII covenant book. I think there's a total of five origin stories for VII now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Clan Akhud, the Russian houses, and possibly some Sanctified experiment gone wrong. What are the other two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T06:52:20-07:00","id":933398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933380#post933380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, a human forcefully draining a vampire is one of the legendary origins of VII. At least, its one of the three in the VII covenant book. I think there's a total of five origin stories for VII now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's suppose to be a one time, unique event that is quasi mythical. Its not suppose to be an everyday type of thing.<br /> <br /> I would discourage the human drains a vampire and becomes a vampire thing. That being said, I think its fine for a major plot point/twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:06:02-07:00","id":933403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933365#post933365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can forcibly drain another Kindred's Vitae, so I don't think the, it doesn't leave the vampires body unless they want it to is a valid argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>By normal means, sure. Another vampire contesting your domain over your blood is not the same that trying to stab it's cold, dead heart for a biopsy. Syringes hardly qualify for the same purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:19:30-07:00","id":933407,"title":"","content":"&quot;Vampires can forceablly drain another Kindred's Vitae, so I don't think the, it doesn't leave the vampires body unless they want it to is a valid argument.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's several magic powers that pull vitae from kindred involuntarily, but a normal human can't do it. The very process of pulling blood and life energy from a living creature and converting it to vitae suitable for vampire consumption or as a material component for magical Beast-imbued powers is supernatural in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-18-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T09:02:56-07:00","id":933443,"title":"","content":"The Kindred fighting style's fluff lets you expel Vitae via massive trauma that the blood can't compensate for. I imagine just sticking a heart shunt in wouldn't work, but something like the extraction table from Blade, or several dialysis machines running simultaneously, or creative centrifuging, or dismemberment and... juicing, would at least tax a kindred's ability to play Vitae keep-away. <br /> <br /> I doubt it would result in another vampire, but I love seeing that parasite relationship run backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T10:11:25-07:00","id":933466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933393#post933393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Clan Akhud, the Russian houses, and possibly some Sanctified experiment gone wrong. What are the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div> Something that came later during the Fall from Rome era (I'm unclear on the details myself) and the new God-Machine theory in the new core book. At least those are the ones I'm familar with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933398#post933398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that's suppose to be a one time, unique event that is quasi mythical. Its not suppose to be an everyday type of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> So was Dracula's spontaneous Embrace thing. Now, he's seen as nothing more than an uplifted revenant than something unique. I don't think we need to make this into a sacred cow, especially when the Curse in 2e really, really wants to spread to everyone it can touch, like some kind of disease.<br /> <br /> The point really boils down to this - its possible that it already happened once, so it might happen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T12:31:37-07:00","id":933527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=933380#post933380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, a human forcefully draining a vampire is one of the legendary origins of VII. At least, its one of the three in the VII covenant book. I think there's a total of five origin stories for VII now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven, actually...!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:52:23-07:00","id":934069,"title":"","content":"But aren't there quite a lot of stories about ghouls keeping Kindred staked to use them as a constant source of vitae? I also remember the <b>Blutmanschienen</b> some kind of fridge like device mentioned in the Gangrel clanbook which was basically a vitae keg. Are these not canon anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:50:31-07:00","id":934149,"title":"","content":"I dont know if there are stories about ghouls keeping vampires staked to feed off of them, but again. Humans aren't equipped to just normally pull vitae from a vampire. If a vampire was staked, it would probably try to heal and burn the vitae it had anyway. If there is no vitae, they couldnt really give it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T16:41:45-07:00","id":934171,"title":"","content":"My original thought was since the human was still alive it might result in a mortal that could use discipline powers while being unaffected by sunlight but i guess i was way off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T17:44:21-07:00","id":934208,"title":"","content":"A mortal, who is still alive and can use discipline powers while being unaffected by sunlight is.... a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T18:17:25-07:00","id":934225,"title":"","content":"Worth keeping in mind that the human who devoured his vampire regnant in one of the origin stories for the VII, thereby 'self Embracing' was not a mere human, but a ghoul who had already lived several centuries.<br /> <br /> Also that we do have posthumous embraces, that occur when someone has died with Vitae in them or after having Vitae in them. It's possible said human, after eating a hundred and something pound vampire corpse, would die shortly thereafter, such as from their stomach rupturing, then rise as a vampire. As has been noted, you couldn't just 'drain' the vampire, since the Vitae is not in its blood, nor where it doesn't want it to be, such as in the mouths of random cannibals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-19-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T20:31:58-07:00","id":934258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934208#post934208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mortal, who is still alive and can use discipline powers while being unaffected by sunlight is.... a ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThanks for letting me know, i thought ghouls were just human servants of vampires who are addicted to their blood. i had no idea they had powers as well <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:44:40-07:00","id":934366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934258#post934258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThanks for letting me know, i thought ghouls were just human servants of vampires who are addicted to their blood. i had no idea they had powers as well</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah there's a huge difference. A ghoul is a human with a vitae pool and access to disciplines as well as unique merits. A person who is just addicted to a vampire's blood is just blood-bound. Ghouls don't have to be blood bound and in fact there are ghoul families (naturally occuring ghouls) that are immune to the vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:08:57-07:00","id":934375,"title":"","content":"According to Dark Eras, Dracula was cursed with vampirism by the God-Machine, so he is definitely more than an uplifted revenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:59:15-07:00","id":934386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934375#post934375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Dark Eras, Dracula was cursed with vampirism by the God-Machine, so he is definitely more than an uplifted revenant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, really? That's a pretty odd to actually confirm exactly what Dracula is and what his origins are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:56:58-07:00","id":934404,"title":"","content":"*Shrugs* Core book calls him &quot;the most famous revenant.&quot; The Rites details him falling in combat to a vampire and blood spilling into his mouth, and later diablarizing vampires. &quot;Cursed by God&quot; is a common theme with Dracula, after all, and the G-M is the closest equivalent. Even if it was true that the G-M &quot;cursed&quot; Dracula, the angels usually do that by manipulating the real world events in subtle ways rather than dragging someone bodily to a facility. So, even if God chose to manipulate events to turn Drac into a vampire (or, just as possible, it was part of the Infrastructure to create an Output, then promptly ignored), we're likely still talking about turning him into a regular revenant than something special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:34:36-07:00","id":934486,"title":"","content":"well, I can assume that Cheiron may have the necessary technology to drain vampire of blood or transplant &quot;vampire fangs&quot; for one of its agents, but yeah- regular mortals shouldn't do it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:37:17-07:00","id":934487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934386#post934386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, really? That's a pretty odd to actually confirm exactly what Dracula is and what his origins are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very surprised someone would take the section as a confirmation that the God-Machine made Dracula.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras p90, 'Dracula falls in battle and awakens in death. He feasts on the fallen, drinking the blood of Wallachian, Moldavian, and Ottoman alike. When morning breaks he is forced to flee from the blinding sun. As it burns his flesh, Dracula realizes he has underestimated the true nature and scale of his enemy. Finally, he names his adversary.<br /> It is God. God, who sent the Ottomans to claim his homeland, who turned his own brother against him, who united the boyars of Wallachia against their Voivode, and, as a final act of cruelty, cursed him with undeath. Dracula vows to defy God.'<br /> <br /> Even if one took God to mean the God Machine, there's nothing that says the God Machine was involved with it at all, though a line a few pages before explains that there were cultists among those he killed. His desire for vengeance seems a personal thing, not something driven by, say, a message taking responsibility for his becoming a vampire. I believe the Rites of the Dragon went into it further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:25:04-07:00","id":934503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934366#post934366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah there's a huge difference. A ghoul is a human with a vitae pool and access to disciplines as well as unique merits. A person who is just addicted to a vampire's blood is just blood-bound. Ghouls don't have to be blood bound and in fact there are ghoul families (naturally occuring ghouls) that are immune to the vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDo they have weaknesses like vampires have sunlight and aggravated damage from fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:28:54-07:00","id":934504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934503#post934503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDo they have weaknesses like vampires have sunlight and aggravated damage from fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They need to take Vitae at least once a month to maintain their agelessness and powers, this usually leads to blood bondage. They cannot create Vitae on their own, and need it fed to them, so it pays to either have a generous regnant or Physical Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T08:59:46-07:00","id":934516,"title":"","content":"If you read the preceding text, you'll see that Dracula waged a twenty-year crusade against agents of the God-Machine (although he didn't know the name or nature of his adversary, only realizing that this adversary was &quot;God&quot; after being turned into a vampire). This, combined with the fact that the section in question is all about Demon: the Descent, led me to the conclusion that the God-Machine cursed Dracula. Granted, it could have been a coincidence and Dracula could have been created the same way as a normal revenant, but the fact that Requiem 1e was adamant that Dracula had been cursed by God, plus the fact that I love crossovers, made me decide that at least in my campaign, Dracula was indeed cursed by the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T10:41:03-07:00","id":934585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934516#post934516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the preceding text, you'll see that Dracula waged a twenty-year crusade against agents of the God-Machine (although he didn't know the name or nature of his adversary, only realizing that this adversary was &quot;God&quot; after being turned into a vampire). This, combined with the fact that the section in question is all about Demon: the Descent, led me to the conclusion that the God-Machine cursed Dracula. Granted, it could have been a coincidence and Dracula could have been created the same way as a normal revenant, but the fact that Requiem 1e was adamant that Dracula had been cursed by God, plus the fact that I love crossovers, made me decide that at least in my campaign, Dracula was indeed cursed by the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he could have been somehow tainted and raised on account of said taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T11:05:52-07:00","id":934603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934516#post934516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the fact that Requiem 1e was adamant that Dracula had been cursed by God, plus the fact that I love crossovers, made me decide that at least in my campaign, Dracula was indeed cursed by the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has interesting implications. What could compel the G-M to upset the status quo by introducing a rebellious element into undead society? Was it just a long-term plan to harvest a single angry human as a vampire element, or was it honestly trying to inflict a fists-raised-to-a-weeping-sky-<i>noooooo</i> condemnation onto a threat to its plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:45:03-07:00","id":934657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/933145-what-happens-when?p=934503#post934503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDo they have weaknesses like vampires have sunlight and aggravated damage from fire?</div> </div> </div> </div> At this point I have to question if you have actually read the ghoul section in the vampire book. It's not even that long. All things you would know had you read it.<br /> <br /> Second someone said they need vitae once a month. That is not entirely true either. They need to spend vitae once a month to maintain their status. They can hold as much as their stamina ( +resilience ) allow them too. So 5 stamina and 5 resil they would only need to be fed once every 10 months ... That is if they didn't spend any on healing or powers or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:46:10-07:00","id":935133,"title":"","content":"Dracula believed that he was cursed by God, which he understood through the prism of being a Christian prince in life. Because he was/is a charismatic badass, other vampires believed him. And it's definitely not something we should rule out.<br /> <br /> Does &quot;God&quot; mean &quot;the God-Machine?&quot; That really depends on what you believe. What Dracula himself believed when he was last seen... well... we don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-21-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:24:06-07:00","id":935397,"title":"","content":"Ghouls stealing vitae from vampires is a classic trope. That said, if you are asking if humans can diablerize, the answer is probably no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}